---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { stats, hero, played, brief, series, neverPlayed } from '../data/gaming';

// Single-series magnitude chart: one hue, linear scale, no legend — the
// heading names the measure. Counter-Strike 2 is excluded and shown as a
// hero number instead; on a shared axis it would flatten every other bar
// to a sliver.
const max = Math.max(...played.map((g) => g.hours));
const bars = played.map((g) => ({ ...g, pct: (g.hours / max) * 100 }));
---

<Base
  title="Gaming"
  description="Thirteen years on Steam: 174 games, 5,587 hours, and one of them accounts for four fifths of it."
>
  <article class="prose gaming">
    <p class="kicker">Gaming</p>
    <h1>Thirteen years, 174 games, one obsession.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      Steam has kept a precise record since September 2013 — thirteen years of
      it. Long campaigns, a lot of strategy, and one competitive shooter I have
      never really stopped playing.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule-line" />

    <section>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt class="tabular">{stats.owned}</dt><dd>games in the library</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="tabular">{stats.played}</dt><dd>played</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="tabular">{stats.hours.toLocaleString()}</dt><dd>hours played</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="tabular">{stats.memberSince.split(' ')[1]}</dt><dd>on Steam since</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="aside">
        Those hours are {stats.days} days — near enough eight months of
        continuous play, spread across thirteen years.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule-line" />

    <section class="hero-stat">
      <p class="label">Where it all went</p>
      <p class="hero-num tabular">{hero.hours.toLocaleString()}<span class="hero-unit">hours</span></p>
      <p class="hero-game">{hero.game}</p>
      <p class="hero-note">
        <strong>{hero.share}% of everything.</strong> Every other game I have
        ever played, added together, comes to about a fifth of this one. Last
        played {hero.lastPlayed}, which is to say it never really stopped.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule-line" />

    <section class="u-wide">
      <p class="label">Everything else, by hours</p>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Counter-Strike is left off this chart on purpose — on a shared axis it
        turns every other bar into a sliver.
      </p>
      <ol class="chart">
        {bars.map((g) => (
          <li class="row">
            <span class="row-name">{g.name}</span>
            <span class="row-bar" title={`${g.name} — ${g.hours} hours, last played ${g.last}`}>
              <span class="row-fill" style={`width:${g.pct}%`}></span>
            </span>
            <span class="row-val tabular">{g.hours}</span>
            <span class="row-last">{g.last}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="label">Then everything under ten hours</p>
      <ul class="chips">
        {brief.map((n) => <li class="chip">{n}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule-line" />

    <section class="u-wide">
      <p class="label">Series I keep going back to</p>
      <ol class="series">
        {series.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <div class="s-head">
              <span class="s-name">{s.name}</span>
              <span class="s-meta tabular">{s.titles} titles · {s.hours} hrs</span>
            </div>
            <p class="s-note">{s.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule-line" />

    <section>
      <p class="label">Next up</p>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Thirteen years of sales have built a good queue. These are the ones I
        actually intend to get to.
      </p>
      <ul class="chips">
        {neverPlayed.map((n) => <li class="chip chip--next">{n}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .gaming { padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem) 0 0; }
  .sec-lede { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 58ch; }
  .aside {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-style: italic;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  /* ---- stat tiles ---- */

  .stats {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(8rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.4rem 1.8rem;
  }
  .stats dt {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  .stats dd {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  /* ---- hero number ---- */

  .hero-stat { padding: 0.4rem 0; }
  .hero-num {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 5.4rem);
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero-unit {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-left: 0.6rem;
  }
  .hero-game {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }
  .hero-note {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 54ch;
  }
  .hero-note strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---- bar chart ---- */

  .chart { list-style: none; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 15rem) 1fr 3.4rem 5rem;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.34rem 0;
  }
  .row-name {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .row-bar {
    height: 9px;
    background: var(--rule-soft);
    border-radius: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .row-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
  }
  .row-val {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-align: right;
  }
  .row-last {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  /* ---- series ---- */

  .series { list-style: none; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .series li {
    padding: 0.95rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
  }
  .series li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  .s-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .s-name { font-size: 1.14rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .s-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .s-note { margin-top: 0.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  /* ---- chips ---- */

  .chips {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }
  .chip {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 0.28rem 0.66rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .chip--next { color: var(--ink-soft); border-color: var(--rule); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 3.2rem;
      gap: 0.3rem 0.7rem;
    }
    .row-name { grid-column: 1; }
    .row-val { grid-column: 2; }
    .row-bar { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .row-last { display: none; }
    .row { padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  }
</style>
